  "Question": "It takes \\(5\\) seconds for a clock to strike \\(6\\) o’clock beginning at \\(6{:}00\\) o’clock precisely. If the strikings are uniformly spaced, how long, in seconds, does it take to strike \\(12\\) o’clock?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(9\\dfrac13\\)",
    "B": "\\(10\\)",
    "C": "\\(11\\)",
    "D": "\\(14\\dfrac23\\)",
    "E": "none of these"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The first strike occurs precisely at the starting time, so the elapsed time comes from the gaps between strikes. Six strikes have \\(6-1=5\\) gaps. Since these equal gaps take \\(5\\) seconds altogether, each gap lasts \\(5\\div5=1\\) second.\n\nTwelve strikes have \\(12-1=11\\) gaps, so they take \\(11\\cdot1=11\\) seconds. The answer is \\(\\boxed{11}\\), choice C.",
